  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="99db61df-fb6f-5ebd-a53f-9662dd07b54a" activityNameId="262a134c-5544-5c4c-8271-f2b2d02c4606" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">MOX fuel element for LWR, at nuclear fuel fabrication plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: MOX fuel element for LWR, at nuclear fuel fabrication plant
The data should be considered as an approximation, because they describe the operation of a UO2 fuel fabrication plant, for lack of specific information. Only radioactive emissions to air and water have been taken from the few data avalable on the Hanau plant (closed). The MOX fuel is made of plutonium from reprocessed spent fuel and depleted uranium from enrichment of fresh uranium. The environmental burdens from reprocessing are in this study entirely allocated to the spent fuel, the burdens from enrichment entirely allocated to the enriched uranium. Hence, the MOX fuel is neither directly charged of reprocessing nor of enrichment, but the fuel chain consistently takes into account the total emissions form these two steps.    ;
UUID: 1105af2e-20e3-3297-b5f8-c9d854f6aec1
The module uses the same data set of a UO2 fuel fabrication plant.
Location: North American and European conditions
Technology: No explicit information on operation of current MOX facilities; data reflect UO2 fuel fabrication plants operating in the 1980s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1105af2e-20e3-3297-b5f8-c9d854f6aec1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
